r b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/385893-dark-eras-hollow-disquiet-wasteland?p=386932#post386932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, on a broader note, I think it's actually brilliant we have a Lineage with an explicit sell-by date. Maybe Hollow only appear and can be Redeemed during periods of famine and drought anywhere...mostly because I want there to be hope for the survivors of the rains.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, I must agree with that- especially because of the consequences. I mean, most of the Hollows has either found New Dawn or died out when the rains came. Whether they finished their journey on time or not was something else, but it gives the feeling that the whole world was on a Pilgrimage, and the creation of those prometheans was a part in the attempt to achieve a &quot;New Dawn&quot; for a whole nation. It makes me wander if each of the Lineages has such an &quot;expiration date&quot;, and when the world would redeem itself they would either become human or die out... and who knows how many time it already happened before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachm